1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,502
<i>Bea.</i>

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:07,966
<i>Jordan, I have nothing to do with</i>
<i>whoever is blackmailing Billy.</i>

3
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,884
<i>You're the only one</i>
<i>who has a grudge against Billy.</i>

4
00:00:09,968 --> 00:00:12,220
<i>Jordan, I'm no longer mad at Billy.</i>

5
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:13,430
<i>I'm fine now. I'm not mad anymore.</i>

6
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:15,765
<i>- If it wasn't you, then who?</i>
<i>- I don't know!</i>

7
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:17,183
<i>I don't know!</i>

8
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,644
<i>Maybe they're not actually</i>
<i>targeting Billy at all.</i>

9
00:00:19,728 --> 00:00:21,646
<i>Maybe someone's just using</i>
<i>Billy against you.</i>

10
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:22,647
<i>Think about that too.</i>

11
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:28,862
- [EMOTIONAL MUSIC]
- [RAIN DRIZZLING]

12
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:37,954
<i>What happened to you?</i>

13
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,042
<i>I'm just tired.</i>

14
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:45,879
<i>I used to think</i>

15
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,299
<i>that if you were a good person,</i>

16
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:52,135
<i>life would be easy.</i>

17
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:55,597
<i>But being a good person is actually hard.</i>

18
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:01,686
<i>Especially when the world</i>
<i>isn't good to you either.</i>

19
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:04,856
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't protect you.</i>

20
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:07,150
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>It's okay.</i>

21
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,612
<i>What's important</i>

22
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:13,073
<i>is that you're here.</i>

23
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:15,325
[BILLY] <i>From now on…</i>

24
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:21,998
<i>I'll take care of you and protect you.</i>

25
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:28,630
[JORDAN] <i>This necklace…</i>

26
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:31,508
<i>My mom was wearing it</i>
<i>the last time I saw her.</i>

27
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:33,134
<i>The day she died.</i>

28
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:36,095
<i>But it ended up with Karen,</i>
<i>my dad's partner.</i>

29
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:37,806
<i>Billy, look.</i>

30
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,559
<i>She's the one in the video.</i>
<i>That's Karen, not Bea.</i>

31
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,436
<i>I remember that dress.</i>

32
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,522
<i>I can't say for sure</i>

33
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:48,358
<i>if Dad had anything to do with</i>
<i>what happened to Mom.</i>

34
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,777
<i>But if that's really her necklace…</i>

35
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:54,322
<i>how did it end up with Karen?</i>

36
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:09,129
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

37
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:13,443
You think we can still convince
the advertisers who backed out?

38
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:15,486
Nah. For me?

39
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:17,780
We should be forward ever, backward never.

40
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,741
Let's find someone else!

41
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:22,660
- They left us.
- I agree.

42
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:25,496
I think instead of replacing
our advertisers,

43
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:29,500
we need to focus on making LoveList
impossible to ignore.

44
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,669
Then they'll be the ones
to approach us, right?

45
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:35,465
Period. Hashtag, know your worth.

46
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:40,386
But, guys, we still need ads. Sponsors.

47
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:42,639
Okay.

48
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:46,684
But if we don't want to consider
big brands for now,

49
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:50,939
why don't we go for
smaller local brands instead?

50
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:54,150
We can pitch to, like, several SMEs.

51
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:57,695
Hmm. Well, I can provide you
with market research.

52
00:03:57,779 --> 00:04:00,281
- Okay.
- Sorry, team.

53
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:03,201
Future mommy will be
working from home for now.

54
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:05,495
But I do have a suggestion.

55
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:11,918
Why don't you open a partnership
with restaurants and cafés?

56
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:16,673
You can also offer some perks
for LoveList users.

57
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:21,761
- Is that good?
- Nice. That's a good idea. [CHUCKLING]

58
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:24,097
[TONI GIGGLES] That's good.

59
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,432
Oh, Billy.

60
00:04:27,141 --> 00:04:29,769
Here's my medical certificate.

61
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:32,647
I'm sorry I couldn't come to work.

62
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,483
Sorry if I'm butting in on your meeting.

63
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:37,360
I just wanted to help.

64
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,493
[CLEARS THROAT] Guys…

65
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:49,914
I know I haven't been myself lately.

66
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:55,920
I let my anger consume me,

67
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,923
and I dragged you all down with me.

68
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:02,135
I hurt you.

69
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:05,972
And I'm… I'm so sorry.

70
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:11,644
I wasn't seeing the big picture.

71
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:13,604
It's not true that

72
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:16,107
I was doing it all on my own.

73
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,650
No.

74
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:21,195
Because you're all here
through every struggle.

75
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:23,823
Just to keep this company afloat.

76
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:26,951
Thank you for putting up with me.

77
00:05:29,787 --> 00:05:33,124
LoveList isn't just a company.

78
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:34,208
We all know that.

79
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:38,629
We worked hard for this.
This is our family.

80
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:43,718
So we will fight for it whatever it takes.

81
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:48,890
Chief?

82
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:52,727
Bea is here.

83
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:58,274
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,328
Oh.

85
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:12,246
What's a criminal doing here?

86
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,291
Uh, Billy…

87
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:16,876
I just wanted to make it clear

88
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:20,546
that I have nothing to do with
the blackmail you're getting.

89
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,299
I came here because…

90
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,344
I want to help.

91
00:06:26,427 --> 00:06:29,806
I know that I've done you
and LoveList wrong.

92
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:31,974
I'm not denying that.

93
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:34,310
But I swear, this one isn't on me.

94
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:36,270
I just want to help.

95
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:37,730
You want to help me?

96
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:41,400
Yes. I'll do anything. Just tell me.

97
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:43,861
Wow!

98
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:46,572
Let's give this liar a round of applause!

99
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:47,657
[EMPLOYEES CLAPPING]

100
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,700
Great acting!

101
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:54,831
After all you've done,
you want to help me?

102
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,165
For what?

103
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:58,042
To pretend that you've changed?

104
00:06:58,126 --> 00:06:59,961
Billy, that's not it.

105
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:03,965
I want to help to prove to you
that I really have changed.

106
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:06,300
No. You don't have to prove anything.

107
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:08,594
I won't believe anything you say anyway.

108
00:07:09,178 --> 00:07:13,015
The person you are right now?

109
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:16,185
You're a nobody.

110
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:18,187
And that's all you'll ever be.

111
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,314
Billy, please believe me.

112
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:23,109
I don't mean any harm.

113
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:27,113
Is that so? Oh, all right!

114
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:30,408
Let's list down all the things you did!

115
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:34,871
First, how you trespassed into our home.

116
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:36,080
Do you remember?

117
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:38,833
Then you stole my shoes.

118
00:07:38,916 --> 00:07:40,793
God, Bea!

119
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:42,503
It was just shoes!

120
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:44,422
You could've just asked me
to buy you a pair!

121
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:46,048
What else did you steal?

122
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:47,967
Oh, right. My LoveFeast idea.

123
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:50,553
Also our list of investors.

124
00:07:50,636 --> 00:07:54,640
Then you blackmailed
one of our biggest investors!

125
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:56,225
And for what?

126
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:58,603
To bring our company to the ground?

127
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:03,065
To leave these employees without a job?

128
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,358
That's her, everyone!

129
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:07,778
The one who almost cost you your jobs!

130
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:09,697
- Billy, that's enough.
- No!

131
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,157
You wanted this, right?

132
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:13,701
This is all you've ever wanted!

133
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:17,663
You put my life in danger.

134
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:21,042
You put my family in danger.

135
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:24,587
Even my friends. Even Jordan!

136
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:29,717
My house burned down because of you
and your psychotic mother!

137
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,971
Don't call my mother psychotic.

138
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,640
Oh, but wait!

139
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:37,683
You know what's funny?

140
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:40,770
That no matter how much
you try to get back at me,

141
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:43,481
your mother still loves
your sister more than you.

142
00:08:43,564 --> 00:08:45,316
Was it Abi?

143
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,692
Abi, right?

144
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:51,030
The name you used to try and be like her?

145
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,991
But let's face it.

146
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:58,287
You can steal her name.

147
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:00,915
You can copy her life.

148
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:06,003
But you will never be your sister.

149
00:09:10,091 --> 00:09:12,468
And you will never be me.

150
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:15,721
Your "Billy Idol."

151
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:20,893
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,146
You're just Bea.

153
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:27,733
The jealous Bea.

154
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:30,611
The Bea who gets off
on ruining other people's lives

155
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,572
because no one loves her.

156
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:34,490
Oh, no.

157
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:36,867
There's one person who loved you.

158
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:37,952
Caloy.

159
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,831
But he's gone now too,
also because of you!

160
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:43,332
I said enough!

161
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,711
You're crossing the line.

162
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:50,798
Don't act like you never did
anything wrong in your life.

163
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:53,301
I wanted to change and help,
but you refused.

164
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:57,763
You'd rather I stay evil?
Well, all right, then.

165
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:59,599
I'll give you what you want.

166
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:02,852
And I'll make sure you regret it, Billy.

167
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:06,856
Exciting!

168
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,984
I can't wait.

169
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:16,532
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:28,210
[BILLY ON VIDEO] <i>There's one</i>
<i>person who loved you.</i>

171
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,879
<i>- Caloy.</i>
- Mm.

172
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:31,964
- Who's that?
<i>- But he's gone now.</i>

173
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:35,301
- Bea, Billy's sister.
- [BEA] <i>I said, enough!</i>

174
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:37,219
- [BILLY] <i>That's her, everyone!</i>
- Hm.

175
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:40,264
- Billy mentioned her yesterday.
- <i>The one who almost cost you your jobs!</i>

176
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,808
Wow. Billy even threw her in jail.

177
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:47,438
Billy despises her.
Look, they're trending again.

178
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:51,651
If Billy thinks she's behind the
blackmail, then we're off the hook, right?

179
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:56,947
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

180
00:10:57,031 --> 00:11:00,159
You're meeting with Billy tomorrow.

181
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:02,411
Do you really think
she'll give you the 10 million?

182
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:05,081
Of course. She has no other choice.

183
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:08,459
Her life's falling apart, even LoveList.

184
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:10,795
She won't let me ruin it any further.

185
00:11:10,878 --> 00:11:11,962
[BEA] <i>You're crossing the line.</i>

186
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:16,092
<i>Don't act like you never did</i>
<i>anything wrong in your life.</i>

187
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:18,511
<i>I wanted to change and help,</i>
<i>but you refused.</i>

188
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:22,056
<i>You'd rather I stay evil?</i>
<i>Well, all right, then.</i>

189
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:23,224
Goodness!

190
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:25,643
All right. Get out of here.

191
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:27,269
You might get captured by the camera.

192
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:31,065
[CLEARS THROAT] I'm going to start.

193
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:35,611
<i>Hello, hello, hello!</i>
<i>This is Sassy Karen.</i>

194
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:36,862
<i>We are live again.</i>

195
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:41,784
<i>I'll be selling your favorite</i>
<i>scent products.</i>

196
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:45,621
<i>You got it right!</i>
<i>We have scents from Halimuyak!</i>

197
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:48,582
<i>It's our bestseller.</i>

198
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:52,086
<i>"How much?</i>
<i>Is there a discount?"</i>

199
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:54,088
<i>Yes, we'll give discounts today</i>

200
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:56,340
<i>because we're going to</i>
<i>have a clearance sale.</i>

201
00:11:56,424 --> 00:12:00,261
<i>So just tell me what product</i>
<i>you want me to flex.</i>

202
00:12:00,344 --> 00:12:06,559
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

203
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:23,868
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:47,850
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

205
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:49,310
[PHONE RINGS]

206
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,354
[RINGING CONTINUES]

207
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:54,190
[DISTORTED VOICE] <i>Billy.</i>

208
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:56,775
I just wanted to remind you.

209
00:12:57,568 --> 00:12:59,945
Meet me tomorrow night

210
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:03,115
<i>at ten o'clock on Gerona Avenue.</i>

211
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:04,950
<i>Bring 10 million pesos.</i>

212
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:09,079
Don't even think about
bringing the police.

213
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,372
Understood?

214
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:12,708
Okay.

215
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,960
I'll see you tomorrow.

216
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:20,132
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

217
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:32,478
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

218
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:54,333
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

219
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:16,647
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:22,319
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:30,077
- Mm.
- Don't push yourself too much.

222
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,912
Baby, don't worry.

223
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:35,165
Your mom and I will give you a good life.

224
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:41,005
You sound so sure
that Billy will give us the money.

225
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,923
You're such a buzzkill.

226
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:46,594
Desperate times
call for desperate measures.

227
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:49,096
So I'm sure that
she's going to bring the money.

228
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,389
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

229
00:14:50,472 --> 00:14:54,268
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:56,228
- Who is that?
- I'll check.

231
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:07,239
Bea?

232
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,533
Mm-hmm.

233
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,451
You're Karen, right?

234
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:14,830
You're Jordan's father's partner.

235
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:16,540
If you're looking for him,

236
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:18,417
I don't know where that bastard is.

237
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,795
Besides, how do you know where I live?

238
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:23,839
Uh, Karen.

239
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:26,091
I have an offer.

240
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:27,343
It's a good one.

241
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:29,470
Offer? W-What offer?

242
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:32,222
Aren't you going to
invite me inside first?

243
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,974
Why should I trust you in the first place?

244
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:35,893
Fine, it's hard to trust me.

245
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:37,478
But believe me,

246
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:39,396
I'm on your side.

247
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,773
I'm your ally.

248
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,192
Okay.

249
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:47,863
I heard Billy and Jordan talking.

250
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:51,033
You're blackmailing them, right?
You're asking for 10 million.

251
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:53,494
I don't really care about your plan.

252
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:59,083
But my favorite sister
is accusing me of doing it.

253
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:02,336
She's saying that I'm behind this.

254
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,879
Oh, really?

255
00:16:04,505 --> 00:16:07,466
Yes. So I ran out of patience.

256
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:11,387
If she wants to think that I'm involved,
then fine, I'll get involved.

257
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:14,390
So we should work together.
Let's make it happen.

258
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:17,142
You know what people say.

259
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:22,606
My enemy's enemy is my friend.

260
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:25,025
So, you're my friends.

261
00:16:26,902 --> 00:16:28,195
You know, we should work together.

262
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:32,199
Because I'm not sure
if Billy would keep her word

263
00:16:32,282 --> 00:16:34,118
and give you the 10 million.

264
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:40,082
I want to offer you a new strategy.
Let's switch it up.

265
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:43,127
Billy has a lot of jewelry at home.

266
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:45,629
I'll help you steal it.

267
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:47,089
I'll help you.

268
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:49,341
But not without a good deal.

269
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,135
You have to give me my cut.

270
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:53,220
No, thanks. You should go.

271
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:54,680
I don't know what you're talking about.

272
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:56,473
Are you sure? Okay.

273
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:59,143
Say goodbye to 10 million and the jewelry.

274
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:00,477
I'll keep it all to myself.

275
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:02,312
- It's like hitting the jackpot.
- [DINO] Karen?

276
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:05,566
- [KAREN] Just go.
- Hey! Wait.

277
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:07,526
Oh!

278
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:12,239
I thought you didn't know
anything. [SCOFFS]

279
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:17,828
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,749
<i>You're okay.</i>

281
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:23,333
<i>You're her sister?</i>

282
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:26,503
<i>Yes, I'm her sister.</i>

283
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:30,632
But whenever something
happens to her,

284
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:32,885
<i>she blames it on me.</i>

285
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:33,886
<i>Gosh.</i>

286
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:35,721
<i>Wow.</i>

287
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:38,432
<i>So it's true that Billy</i>
<i>really despises you.</i>

288
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:41,268
<i>She does. She made me</i>
<i>and my mom suffer.</i>

289
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:43,604
<i>That's why my mom is in prison right now.</i>

290
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:47,441
<i>But now, it turns out that</i>
<i>she's also a criminal.</i>

291
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:52,196
<i>So? Let me in on the gossip.</i>

292
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,447
<i>Is it true?</i>

293
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:57,367
<i>Is Billy the one</i>
<i>who killed Jordan's mother?</i>

294
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:58,702
<i>You're not listening.</i>

295
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:01,914
<i>I already told you that it was her.</i>

296
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:03,624
<i>Oh? Really?</i>

297
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:06,752
<i>We'll divide the jewelry</i>
<i>equally between us.</i>

298
00:18:06,835 --> 00:18:08,712
<i>- Okay?</i>
<i>- Equally?</i>

299
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:10,047
<i>We'll do sixty-forty.</i>

300
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:13,467
<i>You came to me because you</i>
<i>needed my help, right?</i>

301
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,760
<i>That's unacceptable.</i>

302
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:17,846
<i>We're in the same boat,</i>
<i>but you refuse to be equal?</i>

303
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,932
<i>My father has no conscience.</i>

304
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:21,600
<i>Jordan.</i>

305
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:25,354
<i>What matters is, we now know</i>
<i>that he's the one behind this.</i>

306
00:18:25,437 --> 00:18:29,358
<i>Dude, he had something to do with</i>
<i>what happened to Mom.</i>

307
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,069
<i>I know it.</i>

308
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,779
<i>He knows something.</i>

309
00:18:33,862 --> 00:18:35,280
<i>The money is ready.</i>

310
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:37,199
<i>I'm coming with you.</i>

311
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:39,076
<i>No, Jordan.</i>

312
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:42,621
<i>I'll see you later?</i>

313
00:18:42,704 --> 00:18:43,872
<i>Billy.</i>

314
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:49,586
<i>Be careful.</i>

315
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:53,507
<i>Ralph, thank you.</i>

316
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,843
<i>I'll give it back.</i>

317
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:58,554
<i>I just need to show the money</i>
<i>to Jordan's dad.</i>

318
00:18:58,637 --> 00:19:00,722
<i>Billy, I just… I just want</i>
<i>to let you know, okay?</i>

319
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,933
<i>I'm not worried about the money.</i>

320
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,269
<i>I'm worried about your safety.</i>

321
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:07,813
<i>Me too.</i>

322
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:12,359
<i>What if we just report him</i>
<i>straight to the police?</i>

323
00:19:12,442 --> 00:19:14,695
<i>They won't stop accusing me.</i>

324
00:19:14,778 --> 00:19:16,989
<i>Once I get the 10 million,</i>

325
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,615
<i>we're going to call Bea</i>

326
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:22,452
<i>and tell her that we'll</i>
<i>take Billy's jewelry.</i>

327
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,247
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

328
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:27,249
<i>Wish Papa good luck.</i>

329
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:30,210
<i>Just because of that necklace,</i>

330
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,629
<i>your father was the one</i>
<i>who killed your mother?</i>

331
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:35,215
<i>It's not enough proof, is it?</i>

332
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:38,844
<i>You know, I admire</i>
<i>how you support my father.</i>

333
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,305
<i>Well, I get it.</i>

334
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:45,225
<i>He's the father of your child after all.</i>

335
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:47,603
<i>- Get out.</i>
<i>- Look, Karen, please.</i>

336
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,607
<i>My biggest regret in life</i>

337
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:54,860
<i>is that I couldn't convince my mom</i>
<i>to leave my dad.</i>

338
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,529
<i>If I had, she would still be alive today.</i>

339
00:19:57,613 --> 00:20:01,450
<i>I don't want that to happen again.</i>

340
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:02,618
<i>To you.</i>
